-- WA.seg: what each declaration's informal text opens.
-- Notation (opened to expose the shape of a type, "A x", a pair, Id Bool _ true):
--   Cl Iff Cap Sub Eqv tau M scA Meet OTc TH Bar Seg Tr LT OK Tr3 le
-- Computational definitions, opened only where the text says "by definition":
--   idx (index(sup(x, f)) = x) in idx-sup and cor-ind;  Cor in cor-sup (Remark 5.7(c));
--   WA in wa-mk, wa-sig, wa-elim (Def. 5.6(d)).
Meet: Cl
OTc:
tr-B: Cl
TH: Cl
W1:
idx:
Cor: Cl TH
idx-sup: Cl idx
cor-sup: Cor Cl Iff TH
WA: Cl
wa-mk: Cl WA
wa-sig: Cl WA
wa-elim: Cl WA
ch: TH Cl Sub
wa-a: scA Cl TH Sub
cor-step: Cl TH Sub Cap scA tau Meet
cor-ind: Cl TH idx
wa-b: Cl Sub
wa-ind: Cl Meet scA Sub
Bar:
Seg: Cl
rem413a: Cl Sub scA
wa-M: Cl Sub
wa-OK: Cl M
wa-agree: Cl Cap tau Sub Eqv M scA
til-bound: Tr LT OK
cap-le: Cap Cl Eqv Sub OTc Iff
ca-below: Cl Sub M OTc
wa-below: Cl Cap M tau Tr3
eqv-sym: Cl Eqv Iff
rem413b: Cap M Cl Eqv Iff
